ok - --help prints the whole documented contract
ok - FM_PC02_OFFLOAD_DISABLE=1 always runs locally without touching ssh or rsync
ok - a live PC02 LLM lane falls back to a local run without touching ssh
ok - a missing supervising home refuses the lane probe and falls back locally
ok - the offload probe scans the supplied supervising home before checking PC02
ok - an unreachable PC02 falls back to a local run
ok - PC02 missing a required tool falls back to a local run rather than a thinner remote run
ok - a stuck or slow probe times out and falls back rather than hanging
ok - a failed rsync to PC02 falls back to a local run
ok - the captain's personal-use switch falls back to a local run
ok - llama-swap holding a loaded model for any live session falls back to a local run
ok - a healthy llama-swap with no loaded model does not block offloading
ok - an unparseable llama-swap /running answer defaults to a local run
ok - a Windows-wide CPU utilization over the threshold falls back to a local run
ok - a Windows GPU-engine utilization over the threshold falls back to a local run
ok - an unparseable or missing resource read defaults to a local run rather than an idle guess
ok - fm-test-run.sh --pc02-if-idle strips the flag and forwards every other argument unchanged
ok - a remote run returns the suite's own exit code promptly despite a straggler and removes its mirror
ok - a green remote run exits 0, returns its --json artifact, and removes its mirror
ok - a remote suite passes the 7200-second default to its timeout executable
ok - remote jobs preserve both caller forms, default to eight, and allow environment overrides with a script cap
ok - an active PC02 test slot routes a second suite to PC01
ok - a process merely mentioning fm-test-run.sh does not block a free host slot
ok - TERM during a remote run kills the remote suite and removes its mirror
ok - TERM with a transport that ignores stdin EOF still stops the remote suite and frees the slot
